wcb|n|One of a vagabond race, whose tribes, coming originally from India, entered Europe in 14th or 15th centry, and are now scattered over Turkey, Russia, Hungary, Spain, England, etc., living by theft, fortune telling, horsejockeying, tinkering, etc. Cf. Bohemian, Romany. ; The language used by the gypsies. ; A dark-complexioned person. ; A cunning or crafty person	N:1b1q,137,2;1b1e,127,2~1b1e,127,2;1b1q,137,2
wcb|a|Pertaining to, or suitable for, gypsies.	j:1b1q,143,3~1b1q,143,3
